course: dictionary
lesson: 11581
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «Mum said, "Put on your anorak, it's raining."» Here an anorak is clothing, a waterproof jacket with a hood.
explain: «Tom knows every bus route in the city. He's a bit of an anorak about buses.» Nobody is wearing anything here. Tom is very keen on a hobby that many people find dull, so anorak means a person like that, a sort of nerd. The clue is the hobby, not a jacket.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «jacket» fits, it means clothing. If «person who is very keen on a boring hobby» fits better, it means that. Always read the words around the hard word first.
fact: An anorak is a waterproof jacket with a hood, often padded.
fact: In UK informal slang, an anorak is a person who is very interested in a hobby that others think is boring, such as train numbers.
fact: The phrase «put on your anorak» means to put on a waterproof jacket before going out in the rain.
fact: The phrase «a bit of an anorak» means someone is very keen on a dull-to-others hobby.
fact: The plural is anoraks, for both meanings.
exercise: «It was pouring, so Sam zipped up his anorak and pulled up the hood.» What is an anorak here? | A kind of train | *A waterproof jacket with a hood | A pair of wellies | A person who loves boring hobbies
exercise: «Ahmed knows the number of every bus in town. He is such an anorak.» What does anorak mean here? | A bus driver | A waterproof jacket | A kind of tent | *A person very keen on a hobby others find boring
exercise: «Put your anorak on, it looks like rain.» Which word in this sentence is the best clue that anorak means clothing? | your | put | *rain | looks
test: «Dad said, "Don't forget your anorak, the forecast says showers."» What does anorak mean? | *A waterproof jacket with a hood | A person who talks too much | A kind of cake | A bus route
test: Which sentence uses anorak to mean a person who is very keen on a boring hobby? | «The anorak was soaking wet after the walk.» | «She wore her red anorak to school.» | «Put the anorak in the wardrobe.» | *«He is a real anorak about train timetables; he knows them all by heart.»
exam: «Ella's yellow anorak kept her dry, and her brother is an anorak about bus timetables.» What does anorak mean the second time? | *A person very keen on a hobby others find dull | A kind of rain | A waterproof jacket | A type of bus
